WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.050
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.320 --> 00:08.071
[shouts] Hey, are you even listening?

3
00:11.408 --> 00:12.993
RED LIGHT ELEGY

4
00:13.076 --> 00:17.205
What's with that innocent look on your face?

5
00:18.081 --> 00:22.336
Sorry to ask this so suddenly, but can you give me back 3.6 million yen?

6
00:22.919 --> 00:24.504
Instead of those guys.

7
00:24.588 --> 00:26.506
-[♪ tense music playing] -[Satoshi mumbles]

8
00:26.590 --> 00:28.675
I...

9
00:28.759 --> 00:31.470
[debt collector] I'm counting on you.

10
00:31.553 --> 00:33.639
Those guys are the only ones who can pay.

11
00:34.514 --> 00:37.726
Hey! Let go of that idiot. He's just a customer.

12
00:37.809 --> 00:38.810
[tuts]

13
00:40.395 --> 00:42.064
There's no way, right?

14
00:42.856 --> 00:43.857
And you stink!

15
00:44.483 --> 00:47.152
[Chiko's mom] You're really something.

16
00:47.235 --> 00:49.404
He's not paying because he didn't borrow any.

17
00:49.488 --> 00:52.824
Since the husband isn't here, the wife is obviously going to pay.

18
00:52.908 --> 00:54.242
Don't you even know that?

19
00:54.326 --> 00:55.619
Maybe I do!

20
00:55.702 --> 00:59.664
He hasn't come back at all, so he must be wandering around somewhere.

21
00:59.748 --> 01:04.544
We've got a court order here, you know. We're gonna have your account seized!

22
01:04.628 --> 01:07.673
Then take this. There aren't that many bottles here.

23
01:08.173 --> 01:11.677
[sighs] In a lousy little factory like this,

24
01:11.760 --> 01:14.054
that attitude of yours won't cut it.

25
01:14.137 --> 01:17.099
Well, that's just your luck then.

26
01:18.684 --> 01:23.313
Hey! If you can make use of that kid, you can pay me back in one fell swoop.

27
01:23.397 --> 01:27.567
If you master the Zenritsu Zen Massage, you'll be the best.

28
01:28.235 --> 01:32.406
What an idiot. I'm busy here so get out already.

29
01:32.489 --> 01:35.117
[debt collector] You can't act like that towards me.

30
01:35.200 --> 01:40.038
I'm telling you to pay me back the money he borrowed.

31
01:42.165 --> 01:45.085
Well, then, should I smash that "luck" of yours to pieces?

32
01:45.168 --> 01:47.003
I'll marinate it and make gumbo!

33
01:47.087 --> 01:50.424
You're just a pathetic nobody, now get out of here!

34
01:50.507 --> 01:53.176
-Why, you little brat! -Wait a minute.

35
01:53.260 --> 01:55.929
I'll pay some interest, so please forgive us!

36
01:56.012 --> 01:58.640
What are you talking about? You've got no right!

37
01:58.723 --> 02:02.394
Let me handle this! Chiko, you've always been looking out for me.

38
02:02.894 --> 02:07.023
[exclaims] All right then! Let's do this!

39
02:07.107 --> 02:09.151
So, what do you got?

40
02:10.068 --> 02:11.903
-30,000 yen at the store-- -[gasps]

41
02:14.614 --> 02:17.325
-[Chiko] Are you all right? -This is a really dangerous thing.

42
02:17.409 --> 02:20.162
-[gagging] -You'll turn to stone, you piece of crap!

43
02:21.329 --> 02:22.748
Are you okay?

44
02:22.831 --> 02:25.876
[Chiko's mom] Did this guy even use his brain?

45
02:25.959 --> 02:28.628
I don't know. He just ran into me.

46
02:30.088 --> 02:31.423
Anyway, I'll be back.

47
02:34.092 --> 02:36.261
[Chiko] I'm going to call an ambulance.

48
02:37.679 --> 02:38.847
I'm okay.

49
02:40.557 --> 02:42.809
I'm used to pretending to faint.

50
02:42.893 --> 02:46.313
You're quite the performer, aren't you?

51
02:46.855 --> 02:48.774
I can throw up here, but...

52
02:48.857 --> 02:50.233
I can't make a mess here.

53
02:50.942 --> 02:52.861
[Chiko's mom laughs]

54
02:52.944 --> 02:57.032
I'm back. Minako always ends up leaving first.

55
02:57.115 --> 02:59.326
[panting]

56
03:00.202 --> 03:01.453
Is he your new boyfriend?

57
03:03.330 --> 03:06.625
-[Chiko] Don't get the wrong idea! -[yells] Ow!

58
03:07.918 --> 03:09.419
He's not.

59
03:09.503 --> 03:11.087
That really hurt.

60
03:11.963 --> 03:14.049
[♪ light music playing]

61
03:14.132 --> 03:15.342
[Inaba chuckles]

62
03:15.425 --> 03:17.761
-[Inaba] Satoshi, you're acting weird. -Oh, deadass?

63
03:17.844 --> 03:19.763
-Do you know what that word means? -[giggles]

64
03:19.846 --> 03:21.431
Learned it from Chiiko, didn't you?

65
03:21.515 --> 03:23.308
Still saying stuff like that.

66
03:23.391 --> 03:26.603
It's obvious you like Chiko.

67
03:26.686 --> 03:29.731
It's obvious that it's unrequited love, but...

68
03:29.814 --> 03:32.692
-I'm still curious about it. -Just leave it at that.

69
03:32.776 --> 03:36.029
Well, that is true, but I did go to Chiko's house.

70
03:36.112 --> 03:39.950
Huh? I asked her so many times, but she never told me a thing.

71
03:40.033 --> 03:42.702
No, that's not okay. That's a crime.

72
03:42.786 --> 03:45.497
Well, well, never mind that.

73
03:45.580 --> 03:47.958
-Huh? -Did you do it?

74
03:48.041 --> 03:50.252
Don't be quick to say that.

75
03:50.335 --> 03:52.087
We're not just that relationship.

76
03:52.170 --> 03:53.880
We're soulmates.

77
03:53.964 --> 03:58.426
What's with that foreign word? It's scary.

78
03:58.510 --> 03:59.594
What do you mean?

79
04:01.763 --> 04:03.098
Aren't you getting dumped?

80
04:04.140 --> 04:06.685
Chiko seems to still be hung up on her ex,

81
04:07.394 --> 04:09.771
so she'll probably find a new one soon.

82
04:09.854 --> 04:12.607
You need to get her on a date and make a move on her.

83
04:13.984 --> 04:17.112
If she doesn't want to, then I won't be disappointed.

84
04:19.197 --> 04:21.866
Youth is just a fleeting moment.

85
04:30.792 --> 04:32.878
-[rain pattering softly] -[engine idling]

86
04:39.926 --> 04:41.136
Oh, Chiko.

87
04:41.678 --> 04:44.180
-Good work today. You're done already? -Yeah.

88
04:46.266 --> 04:48.643
If you'd like, drink this later, please.

89
04:51.855 --> 04:53.064
Thanks.

90
05:00.572 --> 05:02.699
Chiko...

91
05:04.242 --> 05:05.243
This is...

92
05:05.744 --> 05:09.164
-Hey, shouldn't we go now? -Yeah...

93
05:10.290 --> 05:13.209
Do you think...

94
05:15.420 --> 05:17.839
Could you switch shifts with me the day after next?

95
05:17.923 --> 05:18.924
[Chiko] Huh?

96
05:19.007 --> 05:21.927
-I'm the one who's gonna say that. -Yeah, you're right.

97
05:23.762 --> 05:24.763
Oh...

98
05:25.555 --> 05:26.973
Speaking of which,

99
05:28.058 --> 05:29.726
are you free next time?

100
05:30.894 --> 05:31.895
Huh?

101
05:33.521 --> 05:35.690
[♪ light exciting music playing]

102
05:37.359 --> 05:38.652
[Chiko] Waited long?

103
05:38.735 --> 05:41.154
Oh, no, I just got here.

104
05:41.237 --> 05:43.365
Sorry to bother you on your day off.

105
05:43.448 --> 05:45.742
The senior who opened the shop is annoying.

106
05:45.825 --> 05:49.496
Oh, no, I'm just happy to hang out with you even on my day off.

107
05:49.579 --> 05:50.956
Idiot.

108
05:51.039 --> 05:52.916
BIG ZAM

109
05:52.999 --> 05:54.876
[Chiko] He's got a screw loose,

110
05:54.960 --> 05:57.629
-so don't expect much from his cooking. -[Satoshi] Okay.

111
06:02.759 --> 06:04.302
-[door closes] -[doorbell jingles]

112
06:06.972 --> 06:09.557
Hey, Chiko! Thanks for coming!

113
06:09.641 --> 06:10.642
Over here!

114
06:10.725 --> 06:11.810
Excuse me for coming.

115
06:11.893 --> 06:14.020
-Go ahead and sit right here! -[patting on chair]

116
06:17.816 --> 06:19.985
It's been ages, hasn't it?

117
06:20.068 --> 06:22.696
I didn't even come here for lunchtime.

118
06:22.779 --> 06:26.074
[shop owner] You're full of energy, aren't you?

119
06:27.784 --> 06:31.329
You're not that guy, are you?

120
06:31.913 --> 06:34.666
-Is he within range? -[Chiko] He's within range.

121
06:34.749 --> 06:36.418
Doing a part-time job or you lying?

122
06:36.501 --> 06:38.378
No, I'm working on getting my license.

123
06:38.461 --> 06:40.046
[shop owner] Did you get it?

124
06:40.130 --> 06:43.842
You kept saying "Torutoru," so isn't that a "Torutoru" scam?

125
06:44.509 --> 06:47.137
Yusaku should be coming out any minute now.

126
06:47.220 --> 06:48.972
That's none of my business.

127
06:49.055 --> 06:50.890
[shop owner] You two are a perfect match.

128
06:51.558 --> 06:53.643
Glad things worked out for you.

129
06:53.727 --> 06:57.897
Before Yusaku disappeared, the two of us used to ride around on a Jiz all the time.

130
06:58.606 --> 07:01.484
That time we got into a fight in Hiroshima was a classic.

131
07:01.568 --> 07:05.029
You said you'd thrown 10 guys into a kiln. [laughs]

132
07:05.113 --> 07:06.865
I'd totally forgotten about that.

133
07:06.948 --> 07:09.576
-[shop owner] It was pretty wild. -So?

134
07:09.659 --> 07:12.495
-[Chiko] What kind of place is this? -Oh, that's right!

135
07:12.579 --> 07:14.038
How shall I put it?

136
07:14.122 --> 07:15.498
In a nutshell,

137
07:15.582 --> 07:19.419
I'm serving my original dishes in a dining bar.

138
07:19.502 --> 07:21.921
It was originally supposed to be a snack bar.

139
07:22.005 --> 07:25.633
I'm making a prototype right now, so hold on a sec.

140
07:27.385 --> 07:28.970
[Chiko] A prototype?

141
07:30.013 --> 07:34.350
Well, here's the new Osaka specialty I came up with: Okonomi Ramen!

142
07:35.185 --> 07:38.605
-Hironi, there was a finger in it. -[Hironi] I thought it was just hot.

143
07:38.688 --> 07:39.689
Thanks for the food.

144
07:43.985 --> 07:46.070
[slurping]

145
07:46.154 --> 07:48.990
[Satoshi choking]

146
07:51.159 --> 07:53.036
[Chiko gags, groans]

147
07:53.119 --> 07:55.747
[angrily] What the heck is this?

148
07:55.830 --> 07:59.834
Since you guys are the 14th and 15th guys to try it, now I know it sucks.

149
07:59.918 --> 08:02.504
Yeah, I get it now!

150
08:02.587 --> 08:03.755
What is this?

151
08:05.089 --> 08:07.467
-[Hironi] Come again! -Thank you.

152
08:09.886 --> 08:12.055
He's charging 2,000 yen for that.

153
08:12.806 --> 08:13.932
I'll pay.

154
08:14.015 --> 08:16.893
Wait, I'm the one who got dragged into this.

155
08:16.976 --> 08:18.394
Is it okay?

156
08:19.062 --> 08:21.439
I need a bathroom. I'll be back.

157
08:22.023 --> 08:23.358
-[door opens] -Thank you for the meal.

158
08:23.441 --> 08:26.402
-Hey, you're back! -[Chiko] I need a bathroom.

159
08:26.486 --> 08:30.907
[indistinct chatter]

160
08:34.702 --> 08:35.787
[Ishibashi exclaims]

161
08:36.830 --> 08:41.000
-Hey! Hey, hey, hey! -[♪ tense music playing]

162
08:41.584 --> 08:44.671
Gurosuke, what are you doing here?

163
08:45.547 --> 08:47.841
I called you, but you ignored me, didn't you?

164
08:47.924 --> 08:49.008
You mocking me?

165
08:49.092 --> 08:51.886
-Hey! Hey! -[indistinct chatter]

166
08:52.846 --> 08:54.097
Stop it!

167
08:54.180 --> 08:56.307
Just stop already.

168
08:56.391 --> 08:58.685
-Hey. -I'm not paying you any more money.

169
08:58.768 --> 09:01.396
Huh? Are you kidding me?

170
09:01.479 --> 09:02.522
Hey!

171
09:02.605 --> 09:03.648
-[grunts] -[thuds]

172
09:03.731 --> 09:05.400
What the heck are you doing?

173
09:06.442 --> 09:08.695
What the heck was that for?

174
09:08.778 --> 09:09.821
Huh?

175
09:11.197 --> 09:13.158
-Ishi-chan? -What are you looking at?

176
09:13.241 --> 09:16.536
Hey, why are you fighting in front of my store?

177
09:20.748 --> 09:23.001
You have your eyes set on a cute girl, huh?

178
09:23.084 --> 09:24.878
If you'd like, why not come inside?

179
09:24.961 --> 09:27.755
As an apology, why not stay and have delicious food?

180
09:27.839 --> 09:31.259
-[Ishibashi] Let go of me. -Don't be so rough.

181
09:31.342 --> 09:32.927
Huh? [breathing nervously]

182
09:34.888 --> 09:36.639
-[Hironi] All right! Welcome in! -Pizza?

183
09:37.223 --> 09:38.933
-[Ishibashi] Pizza? -[Hironi] Going for pizza?

184
09:39.017 --> 09:41.728
Looks like someone opened the door.

185
09:41.811 --> 09:44.772
-Are you really okay? -Yeah.

186
09:47.525 --> 09:48.818
I'm sorry.

187
09:48.902 --> 09:51.112
That guy's a loser.

188
09:52.864 --> 09:54.282
[Chiko] See ya!

189
10:07.462 --> 10:09.547
[Chiko] I'll be getting my license soon.

190
10:10.965 --> 10:12.926
Then I'll work for a delivery company.

191
10:15.220 --> 10:16.679
You'd better do your best.

192
10:26.147 --> 10:28.566
[♪ pensive music playing]

193
10:33.238 --> 10:35.323
[indistinct chatter]

194
10:44.249 --> 10:45.875
Oh? Big Brother.

195
10:46.709 --> 10:48.169
-Hello. -Oh.

196
10:48.253 --> 10:50.088
[Satoshi's brother] Hey.

197
10:51.297 --> 10:52.632
[whispers] Lend me some cash.

198
10:52.715 --> 10:55.843
Sayaka wants to go to karaoke. I don't have much money.

199
10:55.927 --> 10:57.971
So, you can lend me some, right?

200
11:00.098 --> 11:01.933
I don't have much money right now!

201
11:06.562 --> 11:09.482
-Let me borrow your bike. -That's okay with me.

202
11:14.821 --> 11:16.489
[Satoshi's brother] What's his deal?

203
11:19.158 --> 11:20.493
[Sayaka] Not sure.

204
11:26.332 --> 11:27.959
Chiko.

205
11:28.042 --> 11:29.252
Chiko.

206
11:30.378 --> 11:31.713
Chiko.

207
11:32.714 --> 11:33.881
Chiko.

208
11:35.258 --> 11:36.509
Chiko!

209
11:36.592 --> 11:39.220
[♪ gentle emotional music playing]

210
11:43.433 --> 11:44.434
[exclaims]

211
11:52.817 --> 11:54.736
[panting]

212
12:25.266 --> 12:27.477
[Chiko] Oh, Satoshi.

213
12:27.560 --> 12:29.896
Hey. [panting]

214
12:31.314 --> 12:33.524
I wanted to see you.

215
12:33.608 --> 12:37.320
[Chiko] What are you talking about? We just saw each other earlier.

216
12:37.403 --> 12:39.572
[chuckles] Most of the day too.

217
12:39.655 --> 12:40.865
I'm sorry.

218
12:42.075 --> 12:45.078
But... I want to talk to you.

219
12:45.161 --> 12:46.204
[Chiko] Okay.

220
12:46.871 --> 12:48.206
Hold on.

221
12:50.375 --> 12:52.460
-[Chiko grunts] -[rattling]

222
13:08.643 --> 13:09.811
What is it?

223
13:18.653 --> 13:19.737
I...

224
13:20.446 --> 13:23.074
like you, Chiko.

225
14:25.887 --> 14:27.305
[Satoshi] Morning already.

226
14:28.723 --> 14:30.141
-Good morning. -Good morning.

227
14:36.230 --> 14:37.815
[Inaba] Oh, Satoshi.

228
14:39.942 --> 14:42.320
Chiko quit.

229
14:42.403 --> 14:43.529
[traffic cone thuds]

230
14:43.613 --> 14:47.074
Didn't you guys work at a different site yesterday?

231
14:47.158 --> 14:52.872
[sucks teeth] She asked me not to tell you until Monday, but...

232
14:52.955 --> 14:55.374
-did something happen? -[♪ somber music playing]

233
15:01.756 --> 15:03.090
Oh, no, no.

234
15:04.508 --> 15:06.093
It's all my fault.

235
15:06.802 --> 15:09.555
It's not your fault. Did you confess?

236
15:14.101 --> 15:17.605
[Inaba exhales deeply, inhales deeply]

237
15:25.488 --> 15:27.907
[♪ somber music continues]

238
15:32.119 --> 15:35.706
ROAD STOP

239
15:39.418 --> 15:40.586
[passerby 1] The road is closed.

240
15:40.670 --> 15:42.129
[passerby 2] Looks like we can't go through.

241
15:45.049 --> 15:46.968
That's a shame.

242
15:52.390 --> 15:55.643
[kids] We're back!

243
15:55.726 --> 15:57.561
[adults] Welcome back!

244
15:57.645 --> 15:59.230
[cook] Okinawa-chan, come for a drink.

245
15:59.313 --> 16:00.439
[kids] Okay!

246
16:00.523 --> 16:02.858
-[kid] See you later! -See you later, guys!

247
16:05.236 --> 16:08.364
Seriously, what's going on?

248
16:08.447 --> 16:09.657
[Satoshi] Yeah.

249
16:09.740 --> 16:12.576
If I hadn't said anything, she wouldn't have quit, right?

250
16:12.660 --> 16:15.121
Even if you said something,

251
16:15.204 --> 16:16.914
there's nothing you can do.

252
16:16.998 --> 16:18.249
The start is what matters.

253
16:18.332 --> 16:20.084
So let's start from there, okay?

254
16:28.968 --> 16:33.014
This is the first time I've fallen in love like this. [sniffles]

255
16:33.097 --> 16:36.475
My heart's pounding so hard, it hurts. [sniffles]

256
16:38.561 --> 16:41.647
[Inaba] I think Chiko was happy too.

257
16:41.731 --> 16:44.150
-How do you know that? -[Inaba] I'm not stupid.

258
16:44.233 --> 16:46.861
No one gets upset when someone says, "I like you."

259
16:47.445 --> 16:50.781
And there's no way she'd just disappear without saying anything.

260
16:51.365 --> 16:52.366
[customer 1] Ton-chan.

261
16:52.450 --> 16:54.160
[customer 2] Ton-chan, wake up!

262
16:54.243 --> 16:55.536
[customers] Cheers.

263
16:55.619 --> 16:58.372
Satoshi, you've got to get a response.

264
16:58.456 --> 16:59.623
Huh?

265
16:59.707 --> 17:01.625
Call Chiko right now.

266
17:01.709 --> 17:04.128
If you don't, you won't rest easy.

267
17:04.211 --> 17:06.005
Wait, but...

268
17:06.088 --> 17:07.131
Huh?

269
17:08.341 --> 17:10.593
Hey, why do you know this by heart?

270
17:20.561 --> 17:23.689
Her phone's turned off. [sniffles]

271
17:27.485 --> 17:29.654
Why don't you go visit her house?

272
17:31.238 --> 17:33.240
That's just stalking, isn't it?

273
17:35.326 --> 17:36.577
Is that so?

274
17:46.420 --> 17:48.422
-[Chiko's sister] What do you want? -[gasps]

275
17:49.131 --> 17:51.759
-Who are you? -Who am I?

276
17:52.760 --> 17:54.428
C-Chiko.

277
17:54.512 --> 17:56.597
Oh, Sis. She hasn't been home in a while.

278
17:56.681 --> 17:58.599
-She hasn't come back? -Mm.

279
17:58.683 --> 18:00.643
Sis, she always lived at home.

280
18:00.726 --> 18:02.728
She hasn't been back for two weeks now.

281
18:02.812 --> 18:05.606
[Satoshi] Oh. Is that so?

282
18:05.690 --> 18:07.900
I wonder where she is.

283
18:07.983 --> 18:11.779
Uh, I don't know. It depends on her mood where she goes,

284
18:11.862 --> 18:13.447
so we've given up looking.

285
18:14.573 --> 18:15.741
Is that so?

286
18:17.326 --> 18:18.327
Thank you.

287
18:18.911 --> 18:19.954
See ya.

288
18:27.628 --> 18:30.881
[Satoshi] Mr. Nagata, I need to talk to you for a second.

289
18:30.965 --> 18:33.008
[Inaba] Today's no good. I'm meeting my daughter.

290
18:33.092 --> 18:35.636
-It's been three years. I want to see her. -[Satoshi] Huh? Huh?

291
18:35.720 --> 18:37.638
Let's go out for drinks sometime.

292
18:50.151 --> 18:53.362
[vehicle approaching]

293
18:53.446 --> 18:54.530
[horn honking]

294
18:55.990 --> 18:58.743
Please wait a moment. I'm tidying up right now.

295
18:59.660 --> 19:01.078
-[honking continues] -What?

296
19:04.165 --> 19:05.624
Chiko?

297
19:07.042 --> 19:10.087
I was getting driving practice, so I can finally get my license.

298
19:10.755 --> 19:11.922
Isn't it dangerous to drive right after?

299
19:12.006 --> 19:13.716
It is dangerous.

300
19:13.799 --> 19:15.009
You went to see me today.

301
19:15.676 --> 19:17.344
So sorry about that.

302
19:18.179 --> 19:19.764
You apologize without thinking.

303
19:20.681 --> 19:21.682
[Chiko sighs]

304
19:21.766 --> 19:23.100
Hey.

305
19:23.184 --> 19:25.227
-[patting on truck door] -Drive with me?

306
19:26.687 --> 19:27.897
A drive?

307
19:29.190 --> 19:31.025
[engine rumbling]

308
19:37.198 --> 19:39.158
Chiko, where have you been?

309
19:40.284 --> 19:46.040
I was in Kyoto, Shiga, Fukui, and Gifu

310
19:46.749 --> 19:48.501
for driving practice.

311
19:52.588 --> 19:54.465
Where are we going now?

312
19:55.758 --> 19:57.843
The beach, maybe?

313
19:57.927 --> 20:00.221
Oh, the beach sounds nice.

314
20:09.021 --> 20:12.399
Why did you blurt that out all of a sudden?

315
20:15.778 --> 20:16.904
Well...

316
20:18.030 --> 20:19.949
I did say it out of the blue,

317
20:20.491 --> 20:22.409
but I've liked you for a long time.

318
20:22.993 --> 20:24.203
-[Chiko gasps] -[tires screeching]

319
20:24.286 --> 20:25.663
[Chiko] Again?

320
20:25.746 --> 20:28.582
-Don't say things like that so suddenly! -I'm sorry.

321
20:28.666 --> 20:30.501
[breathing heavily]

322
20:36.799 --> 20:39.176
[♪ pensive music playing]

323
20:39.260 --> 20:42.263
[Chiko] How long do you plan on working as a traffic worker?

324
20:43.848 --> 20:45.015
[Satoshi] Mm...

325
20:46.016 --> 20:50.771
Even if I quit now, I don't have anything I want to do like you do.

326
20:53.732 --> 20:56.360
But I don't think I'll keep doing this forever.

327
20:57.278 --> 21:00.072
I get yelled at, it gets hot,

328
21:00.155 --> 21:02.908
it doesn't feel good and I'm scared of cars.

329
21:03.951 --> 21:08.038
But lately, I've been able to see you and talk to you,

330
21:09.498 --> 21:11.166
and it's been fun.

331
21:16.130 --> 21:20.009
[waves splashing gently]

332
21:20.092 --> 21:23.262
[Satoshi] Chiko, what's your real name?

333
21:23.345 --> 21:25.514
[Chiko chuckles softly] Why all of a sudden?

334
21:25.598 --> 21:27.016
It's Tomoko.

335
21:27.600 --> 21:30.477
-Use the kanji for "fire under water." -[Satoshi] Huh?

336
21:31.353 --> 21:35.107
I also use the same character for my name, Satoshi.

337
21:35.190 --> 21:36.650
[Chiko chuckles softly] Really?

338
21:36.734 --> 21:39.236
This is fate.

339
21:39.320 --> 21:40.571
Our character's the same!

340
21:40.654 --> 21:42.823
[chuckles softly]

341
21:42.907 --> 21:43.991
[chuckles]

342
21:54.585 --> 21:56.295
As for why I quit,

343
21:57.004 --> 21:59.924
it's because I get too shy when I'm with you.

344
22:01.008 --> 22:02.051
Huh?

345
22:05.846 --> 22:08.474
I was going down an unfamiliar road

346
22:09.850 --> 22:11.936
when I suddenly saw your face.

347
22:15.606 --> 22:17.483
I couldn't help but laugh.

348
22:23.739 --> 22:24.907
Chiko...

349
22:52.685 --> 22:54.770
[♪ gentle music playing]

350
22:56.271 --> 22:57.314
From now on,

351
22:58.857 --> 23:00.943
I'm talking to you casually.

352
23:03.570 --> 23:04.571
Okay.

353
23:05.072 --> 23:07.866
-Don't just say "okay." -[chuckles] Sorry.

354
23:07.950 --> 23:09.827
Don't just say "sorry."

355
23:09.910 --> 23:11.829
-[grunting] -[water splashes]

356
23:12.705 --> 23:13.872
[chuckles softly]

357
23:16.792 --> 23:19.795
From now on, call me Chiko.

358
23:21.547 --> 23:24.967
[chuckling softly]

359
23:30.848 --> 23:35.769
Recommended gourmet food in Osaka Senbayashi specialty: grilled offal.

360
23:35.853 --> 23:37.938
[indistinct chatter]

361
23:38.022 --> 23:39.106
[seller 1] 200 yen.

362
23:39.648 --> 23:41.233
RAW BEEF

363
23:41.316 --> 23:42.693
[sizzling]

364
23:44.278 --> 23:46.780
[Satoshi] Oh, it looks good.

365
23:47.656 --> 23:49.992
-[seller 2] Here you go. -Thank you very much.

366
23:55.539 --> 23:56.582
[Chiko] Mmm!

367
23:57.624 --> 23:59.209
-That's good. -[chuckles] Isn't it?

368
23:59.877 --> 24:01.086
[Satoshi] That's good.

369
24:01.170 --> 24:03.047
TANAHARA SHOP

370
24:03.130 --> 24:05.549
[♪ closing theme music playing]

371
24:35.662 --> 24:38.082
[inaudible]

372
25:08.862 --> 25:10.864
Translated by Samantha M
